cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the original KAHM publications and record the exact version/commit when using this forecasting research artifact. The companion manuscript is an unsubmitted research draft."
title: "KAHM forecasting utility: predictive structure, decoder capacity, and cost"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kumar"
    given-names: "Mohit"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohitKumarRostock/Kernel_Affine_Hull_Koopman_Machine"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software and complete experiment accounting for optional KAHM
  residual corrections to preserved raw-history forecasts, matched affine
  and locality controls, and measured error-cost tradeoffs. The artifact
  retains successful predictions and geometric fitting failures, and
  distinguishes complete controlled experiments from a post-hoc archive
  common-support diagnostic.
keywords:
  - Kernel Affine Hull Machines
  - time-series forecasting
  - predictive representations
  - kernel methods
  - reproducibility
